{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q27132235","formula":"C₁₈H₂₂O₂","hill":"C18H22O2","elements":["H","C","O"],"composition":{"C":18.0,"H":22.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"17β-dihydroequilin"},"descriptions":{"en":"17β-Dihydroequilin is a naturally occurring estrogen sex hormone found in horses as well as a medication. As the C3 sulfate ester sodium salt, it is a minor constituent (1.7%) of conjugated estrogens (CEEs; brand name Premarin). However, as equilin, with equilin sulfate being a major component of CEEs, is transformed into 17β-dihydroequilin in the body, analogously to the conversion of estrone into estradiol, 17β-dihydroequilin is, along with estradiol, the most important estrogen responsible for the effects of CEEs."},"fame":2,"pubchemCid":11954027,"mass":270.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"C[C@]12CC[C@H]3C(=CCC4=C3C=CC(=C4)O)[C@@H]1CC[C@@H]2O","inchikey":"NLLMJANWPUQQTA-UBDQQSCGSA-N","iupac":"(9S,13S,14S,17S)-13-methyl-6,9,11,12,14,15,16,17-octahydrocyclopenta[a]phenanthrene-3,17-diol","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"11954027","atoms":42,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-4.992,"y":-1.114,"z":0.602,"el":"O"},{"x":5.857,"y":-0.048,"z":0.384,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.617,"y":-0.531,"z":0.221,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.012,"y":0.578,"z":-0.668,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.072,"y":-0.506,"z":-0.285,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.873,"y":-1.848,"z":-0.059,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.032,"y":1.713,"z":-0.547,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.548,"y":0.761,"z":-0.368,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.389,"y":0.991,"z":-0.465,"el":"C"},{"x":0.267,"y":-0.505,"z":-0.615,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.353,"y":-1.704,"z":0.154,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.56,"y":-0.22,"z":1.739,"el":"C"},{"x":1.756,"y":-0.362,"z":-0.333,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.002,"y":1.899,"z":0.085,"el":"C"},{"x":1.447,"y":2.053,"z":0.415,"el":"C"},{"x":2.3,"y":0.839,"z":0.154,"el":"C"},{"x":2.623,"y":-1.437,"z"